│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     I changed `rich/console.py` so that record and capture no longer interfere, and submitted the patch.                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     The fix has two parts:                                                                                                                     │
│     - **`_write_buffer`**: segments are now added to the record buffer only when the output is actually flushed (`_buffer_index == 0`).        │
│ Previously they were recorded on every call, including while a buffer context was still open, which could record output more than once.        │
│     - **`end_capture`**: captured segments are now recorded explicitly before the buffer is cleared, since the recording that used to happen   │
│ implicitly no longer does.                                                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     Checks: the record/capture cases in `tests/test_console.py` pass, and the full file passes (98 tests). I did not test the hidden tests for │
│ issue #2563 directly, since the issue text was not provided.                                                                                   │
